  "description": "The half of Rask.Testing that needs Rask.Data, so a component-only test project never pulls in EF Core. await Test.Make<Supply>() is a stored aggregate its rules accept: it calls the aggregate's own factory with a value its rules take for every parameter — a value object sampled from its rules, a row spec, a list of one — makes and stores every aggregate it refers to (a Company, the Tank its id names) through their own factories first, and saves it, rules asked, into the test's database. o.Use(acme) hands it one the test made, o.With(\"parts\", parts) a value of the test's own. Reference it beside Rask.Testing from the test project of an app that stores data.",
